Kent Paul Dolan wrote:
> How would an acceptable replacement NetHack scoring
> system work?

I don't think you're ever going to get something that effectively
weights, say, a 6500 turn ascension vs. a pacifist ascension.

I'd just give 1 point each for milestones, e.g. the list below (just
off the top of my head, so certainly open to debate).  That way scores
still serve as a useful measure to new players as to how they're
getting along; if you wanted, you could change it to 1 point per level
visited and 10 per milestone just to give them a bit more feeling of
accomplishment.  Or however many points--the idea is to make the steps
that actually help you toward winning the game get you points, but put
enough early on that players can reach a few of them early enough to
see progress (e.g. Minetown, Oracle, soko).

All ascensions have the same point score; sort by # of conducts and
within that by time, or vice-versa (or have 2 lists).  On big servers
like NAO, people look more at players' ascension percentages, streaks,
conduct combinations, etc than any individual game so I don't think
you lose much there and at least the top of the list would be a bunch
of pretty skillful games.

